+---
+title: Why we gave a toaster opinions
+reviewed: 2026-10-21
+lifecycle: living
+---
+
+# Why we gave a toaster opinions
+
+*By the Tostr founding team*
+
+When we started Tostr in 2025, every investor asked the same question: why would a toaster <!-- fact:company-founded -->
+need software? Our answer has not changed. Appliances should have opinions. A kitchen full of
+machines that silently follow orders is a kitchen that never tells you your bread is stale. <!-- fact:story-appliances-have-opinions -->
+
+Tostr is the first smart toaster. Say "Hey Tostr", tell it what you want, and it <!-- fact:product-claim-first --> <!-- fact:wake-word -->
+answers back in the personality you picked: Butler if you like manners, Coach if you like <!-- fact:story-breakfast-talks-back --> <!-- fact:personality-butler --> <!-- fact:personality-coach -->
+encouragement, Gremlin if you like being judged. <!-- fact:personality-gremlin -->
+
+Tostr ships with 3 personalities today. This winter that list grows, because Nonna joins in <!-- fact:personalities-count --> <!-- fact:personality-nonna -->
+December: she insists you eat something proper, and she will not toast white bread without
+comment.
+
+We also got faster. A full cycle at level 4 now takes 75 seconds, down from what you are used <!-- fact:cycle-seconds -->
+to, and you still pick from 7 browning levels. <!-- fact:browning-levels -->
+
+The response has been bigger than we planned for. We passed 15,000 pre-orders last month, and <!-- fact:preorders -->
+Tostr now ships to 14 countries. Tostr still costs $129, and Personality Pack is still $4.99 a <!-- fact:countries-shipped --> <!-- fact:device-price --> <!-- fact:plan-pro-name --> <!-- fact:plan-pro-price -->
+month.
+
+If you build things, the API is where this gets interesting: `POST /v1/toast` and your <!-- fact:api-endpoint-toast --> <!-- fact:story-platform -->
+calendar can start breakfast. We cannot wait to see what you make it say.
